 ## Overview
-Panoptic Lifting learns a 3D panoptic radiance field from posed RGB images and machine-generated 2D panoptic segmentation masks, lifting noisy 2D labels into a consistent 3D representation of color, density, semantics, and instance identifiers [S1]. Unlike [Panoptic NeRF](11916-panoptic-nerf.md) or [DM-NeRF](11916-panoptic-nerf.md) which require manual ground truth or coarse meshes, this method requires only pre-trained 2D segmentation outputs, making it robust to in-the-wild scenes [S1]. It sets itself apart by using a linear assignment to resolve 2D instance inconsistencies and specific gradient-stopping techniques to prevent noisy labels from corrupting geometry [S1].
+Panoptic Lifting learns a 3D panoptic radiance field from posed RGB images and machine-generated 2D panoptic segmentation masks, lifting noisy 2D labels into a consistent 3D representation of color, density, semantics, and instance identifiers [S1]. Unlike [Panoptic Neural Fields](20291-panoptic-neural-fields.md) and related methods which require manual ground truth or coarse meshes, this method requires only pre-trained 2D segmentation outputs, making it robust to in-the-wild scenes [S1]. It sets itself apart by using a linear assignment to resolve 2D instance inconsistencies and specific gradient-stopping techniques to prevent noisy labels from corrupting geometry [S1].
 
